 ## Background
 
-New Zealand has one of the highest rates of invasive melanoma in the world — 35 to 45 new diagnoses per 100,000 people per year. Melanoma accounts for 80% of NZ's skin cancer-related deaths.
+New Zealand has one of the highest reported rates of invasive melanoma in the world: 35 to 45 new diagnoses per 100,000 people per year. Melanoma accounts for 80% of NZ's skin cancer-related deaths.
 
